research/frontier-2-judge.jsonl:28:{"id":"cor-urysohns-lemma-closes-the-separation-chain","model":"z-ai/glm-5.2","keep":true,"reason":"Verified every proof step against its cited facts: step 1.1 correctly uses [L1] and [A1] to close the singleton; step 2.1 correctly applies Urysohn's lemma [L2] with P=C and Q={x0} (both closed by given+step 1.1, disjoint by step 1.2) to obtain f with f≡0 on C and f(x0)=1, matching the normalization convention of [L3]; step 3.1 correctly invokes [L3] to conclude complete regularity; step 4.1 correctly adds T1 from [A1] to get Tychonoff=T_{3.5}; step 5.1 correctly assembles the full chain from [L4] (which faithfully restates thm-the-separation-implication-chain clauses 1-5) plus the new arrow. The DC hypothesis is properly stated and inherited through [L2]. Title, statement, and remarks all match what is proved. Cross-references to siblings (cor-a-compact-hausdorff-space-is-tychonoff, fs-every-normal-space-is-completely-regular, ex-sierpinski-space-is-normal-and-not-completely-regular, rem-the-choice-cost-of-urysohns-lemma-and-of-tietzes-theorem) are consistent.","at":"2026-07-28T18:42:05.809Z"}
