research/frontier-2-judge.jsonl:78:{"id":"rem-the-choice-cost-of-urysohns-lemma-and-of-tietzes-theorem","model":"z-ai/glm-5.2","keep":true,"reason":"I verified the remark's choice-cost accounting against the full proofs of every cited item: Urysohn's lemma spends DC at step 12.1 (stringing together finite levels built by lem-finite-choice), Tietze spends DC at step 8.1 (with a genuinely dependent relation), the perfectly-normal-iff theorem's forward direction uses DC at step 5.1 in the shape of AC_omega with a memoryless relation, the converse clauses and the dyadic/continuous-function lemmas are choice-free, the metric theorem is choice-free, and thm-perfectly-normal-implies-completely-normal spends only AC_omega. The one tension — listing thm-a-space-is-perfectly-normal-iff under 'purely by inheritance' when it has its own DC application — is explicitly corrected in the immediately following section, which details the step and its discharge as DC. No false claim, mis-cited dependency, or logical gap remains.","at":"2026-07-28T18:52:33.932Z"}
