items/lem-urysohn-sits-between-hausdorff-and-regular-plus-t1.md-77-
items/lem-urysohn-sits-between-hausdorff-and-regular-plus-t1.md-78-1.2 Assume $X$ is Hausdorff and let $x \ne y$; [A2] gives disjoint open $U \ni x$ and $V \ni y$. [A2, assume-hyp]
items/lem-urysohn-sits-between-hausdorff-and-regular-plus-t1.md-79-
items/lem-urysohn-sits-between-hausdorff-and-regular-plus-t1.md-80-1.3 Assume $X$ is regular and $T_1$ and let $x \ne y$; by [L1] the set $\{y\}$ is closed, so $U_0 := X \setminus \{y\}$ is open by [L3] and contains $x$. [L1, L3, assume-hyp]
